-- חוק דמי מחלה (היעדרות בשל מחלת בן זוג), התשנ"ח-1998 — sections 1, 1א,
-- 3, 4 and 5: up to six days a year an employee may charge to his accrued
-- sick leave for his spouse's illness, a spouse being ill who has become
-- wholly dependent on others for daily activities; up to sixty for a
-- spouse's malignant illness, after a year's work, charged to his sick
-- leave or his vacation as he chooses; that the law adds to every other
-- right; and that the State is an employer like any other. The text is
-- laws/sick-pay-spouse-law.toml, pinned from the live page of ספר החוקים
-- הפתוח; the corpus holds no copy (MMS-601).
--
-- Why it is here: the takanon's §1.25.3.1 restates §§1, 1א and 3 as its
-- clause 5 and cites the law. §2's rules on proving the illness and on
-- notices are the Minister's regulations, not pinned.

IMPORT prelude

@desc What an employee may charge an absence to, as section 1א(א) lets him choose.
DECLARE `what a spouse's-illness absence is charged to` IS ONE OF
    `the employee's accrued sick leave`
    `the vacation days due to the employee`

§ `חוק דמי מחלה (היעדרות בשל מחלת בן זוג) — ששה ימים, ושישים במחלה ממארת`

§§ `1`

-- Up to six days a year of absence for his spouse's illness, charged to
-- his accrued sick leave.
@ref law:1
GIVEN `the spouse is ill as section 3 means` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `days a year section 1 of the Spouse Illness Law gives` `the spouse is ill as section 3 means` IS
    IF `the spouse is ill as section 3 means` THEN 6 ELSE 0

#ASSERT `days a year section 1 of the Spouse Illness Law gives` TRUE EQUALS 6

§§ `1א`

-- (א): after a year with the employer or at the workplace, up to sixty
-- days a year of absence for his spouse's malignant illness, charged to
-- his accrued sick leave or to the vacation due to him, as he chooses. (ב):
-- the days charged under §1 count.
@ref law:1א
GIVEN `months with the employer` IS A NUMBER, `days already charged under section 1` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `days left a year under section 1א of the Spouse Illness Law` `months with the employer` `days already charged under section 1` IS
    IF `months with the employer` AT LEAST 12
    THEN max 0 (60 MINUS `days already charged under section 1`)
    ELSE 0

@ref law:1א
GIVEN c IS A `what a spouse's-illness absence is charged to`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 1א lets the employee charge a spouse's malignant illness to` c IF
    TRUE

#ASSERT `days left a year under section 1א of the Spouse Illness Law` 12 6 EQUALS 54
#ASSERT `section 1א lets the employee charge a spouse's malignant illness to` `the vacation days due to the employee`

§§ `3`

-- For §1, a spouse is ill who fell ill and became wholly dependent on
-- others for daily activities, as the National Insurance Law defines them.
@ref law:3
GIVEN `fell ill` IS A BOOLEAN, `wholly dependent on others for daily activities` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `ill as section 3 of the Spouse Illness Law means` `fell ill` `wholly dependent on others for daily activities` IF
    `fell ill` AND `wholly dependent on others for daily activities`

#ASSERT NOT `ill as section 3 of the Spouse Illness Law means` TRUE FALSE

§§ `4`

-- The law adds to an employee's right by law or agreement and takes none
-- away: for a right measured in one number, the larger stands.
@ref law:4
GIVEN `what the law gives` IS A NUMBER, `what the instrument gives` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `what stands under section 4 of the Spouse Illness Law` `what the law gives` `what the instrument gives` IS
    max `what the law gives` `what the instrument gives`

#ASSERT `what stands under section 4 of the Spouse Illness Law` 60 30 EQUALS 60

§§ `5`

-- For this law the State as employer is like any other employer.
@ref law:5
`the Spouse Illness Law binds the State as an employer` MEANS TRUE
